-- cmd: check
-- exit: 1
-- stderr-not-contains: type 'type
-- stderr-not-contains: call it on the type
-- `m.pure(1)` on an unannotated parameter is not read as a type's method
-- (the trait is of type constructors), so `m` would be a record with a
-- field `pure`, which nothing decides: the function is refused, and the
-- help says to annotate the record or how to write the type parameter.
fn go(m) {
  m.pure(1)
}

fn main() {
  println(go(Option))
  println(go(List))
}
